+  // --- Diminishing-returns state for the transform type search ---------------
+  // The candidate order in txk_map is a prior ranking (ML / heuristic), so the
+  // RD cost of the evaluated candidates behaves like a decreasing sequence that
+  // flattens out quickly. Rather than walking the whole ranked list, track how
+  // the search is converging and stop once it has saturated:
+  //   * num_rd_evals   - candidates that reached an actual RD evaluation,
+  //   * stale_run      - consecutive evaluations that did not beat best_rd,
+  //   * last_rd_gain   - absolute RD improvement of the most recent winner.
+  // A small last_rd_gain relative to best_rd means the sequence has already
+  // converged, so the tolerated stale run is shortened. The same holds when the
+  // winning candidate produced a very compact residual (small eob): the
+  // transform already concentrated the energy and the remaining kernels have
+  // little room left to improve on it.
+  int num_rd_evals = 0;
+  int stale_run = 0;
+  int64_t last_rd_gain = INT64_MAX;
